From b3a89bf9a511fc566af1acff1b919b107d53442d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arch-port <26345330+DrShadow34@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:17:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: v9 index rewrites, geometry shaders with GPU-side
 counts

What the tiler cannot draw, as an index list written by a precomp job
(panlib_rewrite_indices_v9) ahead of the draw:
- VK_POLYGON_MODE_LINE: the three edges of each triangle as a line list
  (no face culling of the edges: CTS rasterization.culling.*_line fail);
- adjacency topologies without a geometry shader: the primitives without
  their adjacent vertices (poly_vertex_id_for_topology()).
With an indirect draw or primitive restart in strips the count is known
on the GPU only: LINE mode then draws filled, adjacency is skipped.

Geometry shaders with indirect draws and primitive restart in strips
(src/poly's GPU-side setup, as Honeykrisp): a device heap (poly_heap,
grown on fault) reset by the first such draw of a batch; restart is
unrolled to a list in it (poly_unroll_restart); panlib_gs_setup_indirect_v9
fills poly's parameters from the draw command and patches the counts of
the vertex / geometry shader compute jobs (queued NOT_STARTED, compute or
null job) and of the layers' IDVS jobs, and the vertex shader's base
vertex / instance / draw ID and per-instance attributes as the indirect
draw helper does. The patched compute jobs are restored before a batch is
issued again. Direct draws forced through this path pass all of CTS
geometry.*; geometry.builtin_variable.in_block.primitive_id_in_restarted
passes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013fD3if93WntovhmD8fGa8C
